meta {
  name: 03 Get Report
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{labReportId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Full report detail — the Test Entry screen's header strip context
  (LABORATORY.docx §4.1), result values, notes (4 categories), attachments,
  and multi-step process if assigned.

  Response also includes `contentSections` (§4.5) — `{ usefulFor,
  interpretation, limitations, remarks, references }`. Each field resolves as
  this REPORT's own saved override (if a technician has ever set one via
  `PATCH .../content-sections`) falling back to the linked `LabTest` master's
  configured default otherwise (Master Data > Add Test > Notes — rich
  text/HTML). Editing here writes to this report only — the shared `LabTest`
  master is never mutated by a technician's edit here, so other orders of the
  same test are unaffected. All 5 fields are editable, each independently
  gated by the branch's TechnicianSetting `is<Field>Editable` toggle (all
  default false). All null when the report has no override saved AND no
  linked LabTest (a panel item, a direct/free-text entry, or a branch-only
  test with no tenant catalogue source).

  Each `resultParams[]` entry also carries `notes`: the parameter's CONFIGURED Note (Master Data > Add Test > Add
  Result > Notes), plain text or null. It is only the default. `parameterNotes: [{ resultParamId, content }]` lists the
  parameters whose Note the technician wrote for THIS report (rich-text HTML, may be empty = "no note on this report",
  saved with `PATCH .../parameter-note/:resultParamId`); a parameter with no entry shows its configured Note.

  404 `LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND` if missing/other-tenant/other-branch.

  **TAT after a transfer (Phase 2).** The limit (Max TAT, processing window, schedule) comes from the entry the holding
  branch works the test with, and the start is the earliest accept among the samples AT THE HOLDING BRANCH (the sender's
  original, still Sent, no longer counts at the receiver). Back at the sender the clock restarts when it accepts the tube
  again.

  Response also includes `notesPrint` - `{ enabled, isPanelMember, excludedSections }`:
  which Notes sections print on this report. `enabled` is the effective
  Branch Setting (Branch Admin > Branch Settings > Technician Settings > Report Printing: the Lab Panel switch when the report's order line is a panel,
  the Lab Test switch otherwise, read from the branch that holds the report; while
  it is off every section prints and no checkboxes should show). `isPanelMember`
  is true for a report on a panel order line (including reports made before the
  per-member split). `excludedSections` lists the section keys
  (`useful_for`, `interpretation`, `limitations`, `remarks`, `references`) left out
  of the printed version. Change it with `PATCH .../note-print-sections`.
}
